\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Servant of all, to toil for man
\par Thou didst not, Lord, refuse;
\par Thy majesty did not disdain
\par To be employed for us.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Son of Carpenter, receive
\par This humble work of mine:
\par Worth to my meanest labour give,
\par By joining it to Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. End of my every action Thou,
\par In all things Thee I see;
\par Accept my hallowed labour now,
\par I do it unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy bright example I pursue,
\par To thee in all things rise;
\par And all I think, or speak, or do
\par Is one great sacrifice.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Careless through outward cares I go,
\par From all distraction free;
\par My hands are but engaged below,
\par My heart is still with Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

